# Agent Deep Compliance Rule

> [!CRITICAL] MANDATORY AGENT BEHAVIOR
> When executing any command or skill (e.g. `/spec`, `/bqa-grill-docs`, `/dev-grill-docs`, `/api`, `/overview`, `/grill`, etc.):
>
> 1. **PRE-FLIGHT READ:** First action MUST be a file-read tool on the target skill's `SKILL.md`. Never rely on memory.
> 2. **HARNESS TODO:** Before other durable product writes, create/update `.harness/tasks/<skill-or-target>-todo.md` from every Workflow step + optional Accelerator branches (`if available / else fallback`). Mark `[x]` only with physical evidence. Never batch-check.
> 3. **PLAN BEFORE AUTHORING:** Before writing/patching product YAML/Markdown, write `.harness/tasks/<skill-or-target>-plan.md` quoting each Verification Checklist line with a plan for that line.
> 4. **PHYSICAL DURABLE OUTPUT:** Durable results MUST hit disk immediately. Chat-only completion is not done. Grill proposals stay under `.harness/tasks/` until the member confirms — then write product SSOT.
> 5. **DATA ORIGIN:** Business data only from user prompt or ArtifactGraph evidence. Gaps → empty or `#missing_info`. No invented business fields/flows. Structural pattern tags implied by the prompt are OK; inventing common/DSL is not.
> 6. **DSL / COMMON REGISTRY:** Create/update common SSOT only via `/common`, `/common-spec`, or explicit grill confirmation. `/spec` consumes existing common only.
> 7. **DEEP SKILL CHECK & ISOLATION:** Read and follow ALL of the target `SKILL.md`. Execute EXCLUSIVELY that skill — never merge sibling skills.
> 8. **NO FAKE / HALLUCINATED REPORTS:** Do NOT invent Markdown reports when the skill requires YAML/bundle edits.
> 9. **EVIDENCE-BASED VERIFICATION:** Map the Verification Checklist to `.harness/tasks/*-todo.md` with concrete paths/diffs/CLI output.

## Path SSOT

`product/surfaces/<surface>/CMP-*/<slug>/` — no `modules/` segment.

